   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p79-guided-block",
     "nodeId": "p79-guided-root",
     "replacement": "The population of kangaroos, $P$ (in thousands), in bushland satisfies\n\n$$\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.1P\\left(1-\\frac{P}{C}\\right)$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the number of years after 2000 and $C$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nIn 2000 there were 15 000 kangaroos. By 2020 there were 60 000 kangaroos.\n\nUse the fact that $\\frac{C}{P(C-P)}=\\frac{1}{P}+\\frac{1}{C-P}$ to show the carrying capacity is approximately 113 000 kangaroos.\n\nFollow these steps:",
