    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p51-exponential-introduction",
     "replacement": "An application of differential equations you have seen before is **exponential growth and decay**.\n\nFor exponential change, the rate of change is **directly proportional** to the current amount $N$: $\\frac{dN}{dt}=kN$, where $k>0$ for growth and $k<0$ for decay.\n\nMore quantity means faster change; less quantity means slower change.",
